European Industrial Gases Association. *Static Vacuum Insulated Cryogenic Vessels — Operation and Inspection*, Doc 224/20, revision of 224/19. [Complete 47-page publication](https://www.eiga.eu/uploads/documents/DOC224.pdf).

Read the complete guide alongside the thermodynamics course. Its scope includes stationary oxygen, nitrogen, argon and helium storage, installation, commissioning, maintenance and inspection. Follow the distinction between stored product, the vacuum insulation and downstream supply.

Cover, contents and selected equipment, insulation, cleanliness and failure-mechanism passages were inspected on 30 October 2026. EIGA grants reproduction with attribution; this is not a blanket CC licence. Installation requirements and referenced standards belong to the document's edition and jurisdiction. The PDF remains external.

